Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:19:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): periodic loop glyph for sessions that own a
 live cron job [daveey]

A session that set up a recurring cron job finished its turn and the sidebar
painted it green (done), although its work goes on periodically. Cron jobs now
record the creating session (owner_session_id: the tool's session id, or the
HERMES_SESSION_ID a 'hermes cron create' subprocess inherits); session-list
endpoints stamp cron_active over the lineage for enabled, scheduled jobs; the
row shows a tiny grey loop glyph in place of the stripe and is treated like a
parked (blocked) row: Cmd-]/Cmd-[ skip it. Only a real prompt (needs-input) beats it.
---
